{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trip record for this trip contains a driver 'arrived' event at 08:43:00, so POL-NS-01 limb (a) is satisfied on the face of the source's own record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "payload.arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The same record shows no boarding event at all - started_at and ended_at are both null - and the trip was terminated by the driver at 08:51:00 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes POL-NS-01(d) expressly recognises; 480 seconds separate the arrival marker from the termination, which is past the 300-second STANDARD minimum, so the trip was terminated at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "payload.cancellation_reason_code",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's only exonerating route on these chat facts, POL-NS-04, fails at limb (a): the chat log holds six entries and every one of them is from the driver or the system, so the rider sent no locating or coordinating message at any point in the waiting window. This is not a gap in the evidence - the log is complete, its six entries match trip_record.chat_message_count of six, and no interval between entries exceeds five minutes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00901", "EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Independently, POL-NS-04 limb (b) is also unavailable to the rider: the driver placed an in-app voice call at 08:47:05, recorded in trip_record.in_app_calls, which rang 22 seconds unanswered and was initiated by the driver, so even if a rider message existed on the chat the driver's call would defeat the limb.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901", "EV-CHAT-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace cannot be turned into an affirmative finding that the driver was outside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. No fix in the trace carries a reported horizontal accuracy, so no fix is shown to be worse than the 25 m filter and, under POL-NS-02, fixes in that state count as evidence of neither presence nor absence. I disclose that this artifact is impaired - weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD - and the claim survives the discount because what it asserts is the absence of a measurement, which impairment cannot manufacture into proof of absence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-05's false-arrival test is not met on the derived facts. The trace's closest approach to the pickup pin is 0.0 m (derived.driver_track.min_distance_m), so the trace contains at least one fix at the pin itself, and no derived figure matches the arrival marker to a position more than 300 m from the pin or to a speed at or above 15 km/h. I disclose the trace's impairment: weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The zero-second dwell that a POL-NS-06 shortfall argument needs is an artefact of sampling, not a finding that the driver did not wait. POL-NS-08(b) is engaged on this very trace - sampling gaps of 180 and 240 seconds exceed its 120-second limb, and the waiting window holds only four fixes against the six that limb requires - so the derived longest qualifying run of 0.0 s cannot alone support a ruling against the driver. I disclose the trace's impairment: weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's account of waiting is corroborated by unimpaired evidence at full weight: the chat log shows the driver announcing his arrival at the lobby at 08:43:00, repeating at 08:45:20 with his vehicle type, colour and plate, and still messaging at 08:50:45 - 465 seconds after the first message and 15 seconds before the 08:51:00 cancellation. That directly contradicts the rider's core assertion that 'the driver never showed up'.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00901", "EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's asserted presence at the pin gains nothing from the GPS record: the source carries no rider track at all, so derived.rider_presence.available is false, and POL-NS-04(c) makes an absent rider track neutral rather than adverse. My point is not an adverse inference but an asymmetry - the driver's account of being at the pickup is corroborated by an unimpaired chat log, while the rider's account of waiting at the lobby is corroborated by no GPS artifact. I disclose the trace's impairment: weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD, the rider_track limb of POL-NS-08(b) being among them.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check cannot be run against this driver. driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is null and driver_profile.completed_trips_30d is null, so neither limb of the check - a trailing-30-day count of 4 or more AND a ratio above 0.08 - is established on this record, and the lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags is not the field the clause reads and may not be substituted for it under POL-GEN-01. Compensation therefore cannot be withheld on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No profile-driven escalation trigger is established. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d, rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are all null on the two profiles, so POL-NS-09(c) and (d) do not bite, and with the anti-farming check undecidable in the driver's favour there is no abuse finding against him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00901", "EV-DPROF-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The traffic advisory artifact is MISSING and carries weight 0.0; its absence is itself citable. I do not assert POL-NS-06(i) against it - the clause provides that asserting a missing advisory triggers POL-NS-09 rather than exonerating anyone - and its absence means no kerb restriction, enforcement operation or closure on this pickup road explains or excuses the driver's position: on his own contemporaneous messages he was simply holding at the lobby, not circling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00901-01", "EV-CHAT-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The disputed charge currently stands and the rider filed this dispute. The ledger shows payment_status CHARGED, total_charged 5.00 and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03 - the filing party's claim not supported and the present state left as it is - leaves the charge in place, which is the driver's outcome. I disclose that this artifact is impaired, weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD, and that POL-NS-08(d) is engaged because 5.00 does not reconcile with fee_schedule's greater-of figure of 4.00 for a STANDARD zone and RYDE_X tier; that defect goes to the amount the platform itemised, not to the driver's entitlement to the fee he waited for.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "If the Judge finds POL-NS-01 satisfied in full on the arrival marker and the corroborating chat, POL-NS-07 provides the driver 80 percent of the itemised cancellation fee, the residual 20 percent being the platform's service fee, and it is only the anti-farming check that can withhold it - and that check is undecidable here, not tripped. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee: POL-NS-04 fails at limb (a), POL-NS-05's triggers are not met, and POL-NS-06's shortfall rests on the impaired trace. I repeat the disclosure that the fare artifact I rely on for the amount is impaired at weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901", "EV-CHAT-00901", "EV-FARE-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "If the Judge concludes the in-geofence dwell cannot be decided at all, the outcome that does not strip a driver who waited is escalation, not refund. The sole evidence for that deciding fact is the trace impaired under POL-NS-08(b), so POL-NS-08's final sentence caps the outcome and sends the case to a human reviewer under POL-NS-09, and escalation is terminal and replaces the monetary ruling: POL-NS-09 holds the disputed fee rather than collecting or refunding it while review is pending, which preserves the present state against the rider's claim for reversal. I disclose the trace's impairment: weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    }
  ]
}
